1,0$Merismodes ///Fruitbodies solitary or gregarious, often closely packed together and form ing large colonies, seated on a subiculum individually bowl-, cup-, or top-shaped, hairy on the outside; hairs long, brown, thick-walled and entrusted with granules except near their thinner-walled, pale usually swollen tips; ///hymenium lining cups smooth, pale. ///Hyphae with clamps. Cystidia none./// Spores hyaline or yellowish, smooth, J-.
1,0 $ Fruitbodies flat bowl-shaped, spores 6-9 x 2-2.5 $ confusus
1,0,n $Merismodes confusus (Bres..) Reid (Fig. 268) ///Fruitbodies gregarious, closely packed together, individually flat bowl shaped, 1-3 mm diam, greyish when young then yellowish brown to dark chestnut brown on the outside, rim fringed with protruding hairs which often end in a bulb; /// hymenium creamy white. ///Spores slightly curved, 6- 9x 2-2.5. ///On dead branches of deciduous trees, including Betula.
1,0 $ Fruitbodics more or less top-shaped, tapered below, spores 8-10x4-5 $ anomalus
1,0,n $Merismodes anomalus (Pers.ex FR.) Sing.(fig 267)///Fruitbodies usually gregarious, closely packed together forming large coloniesT individually cup- to top-shaped, tapered below into a short stalky ochraceous to cinnamon brown and hairy on the outside, with a white or creamy rim, 0.3-0.5 mm diam. ; - hairs up to 150x2-4; ///hymenium lining cup cream or pale ochraceous. ///Basidia 30-40x 5-7T 4-spored, Spores ellipsoid, some slightly curved, 8-10x4-5, ///On wood and bark of deciduous trees, common.
1,2$ Fruitbodies tube- or deep cup-shaped	
2,0 $ Spores 6-11 * 2-2.5 $ fasciculatus
2,0,n$Merismodes fasciculatus (Schw.) Donk. ///Fruitbodies solitary or gregarious* deeply cup- or tube-shaped, up to 1 mm diam., brown on the outside; hairs sometimes curled at apex; ///hymenium cream or yellow. ///Spores 6-11 x 2-2.5. ///On wood of deciduous trees
2,0 $ Spores -7.5 x 3-4 $ ochraceus
2,0,n$Merismodes   ochraceus (Hoffm.ex Pers.) Reid///Fruitbodies deeply cup- to tube-shaped, becoming rust-coloured on the outside, 1-2 x 0.5 mm; ///hymenium creamy white. ///Spores 5-7.5 x 3-4. ///On dead herbaceous stems.